// Binding a listener beyond loopback is the `@http.listen` policy, reached through
// the same function: the wildcard `0.0.0.0` serves the whole network, so it needs
// an explicit grant. The check runs before the socket is bound, so this never
// reaches the blocking accept loop.
! @tcp.listen "0.0.0.0:0" ⟦ |conn|
  ! @tcp.close(conn)?
⟧
